#: ../../source/bl_README.md:10
msgid ""
"**bl** is a storage object for collections of Node Buffers, exposing them"
" with the main Buffer readable API. Also works as a duplex stream so you "
"can collect buffers from a stream that emits them and emit buffers to a "
"stream that consumes them!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/bl_README.md:12
msgid ""
"The original buffers are kept intact and copies are only done as "
"necessary. Any reads that require the use of a single original buffer "
"will return a slice of that buffer only (which references the same memory"
" as the original buffer). Reads that span buffers perform concatenation "
"as required and return the results transparently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/bl_README.md:42
msgid ""
"Give it a callback in the constructor and use it just like **[concat-"
"stream](https://github.com/maxogden/node-concat-stream)**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/bl_README.md:55
msgid ""
"Note that when you use the *callback* method like this, the resulting "
"`data` parameter is a concatenation of all `Buffer` objects in the list. "
"If you want to avoid the overhead of this concatenation (in cases of "
"extreme performance consciousness), then avoid the *callback* method and "
"just listen to `'end'` instead, like a standard Stream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/bl_README.md:57
msgid ""
"Or to fetch a URL using "
"[hyperquest](https://github.com/substack/hyperquest) (should work with "
"[request](http://github.com/mikeal/request) and even plain Node http "
"too!):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/bl_README.md:68
msgid ""
"Or, use it as a readable stream to recompose a list of Buffers to an "
"output source:"
msgstr ""

